Expand description

A widget to display a progress bar.

A `Gauge` renders a bar filled according to the value given to [`Gauge::percent`](struct.Gauge.html#method.percent "method ratatui::widgets::Gauge::percent") or [`Gauge::ratio`](struct.Gauge.html#method.ratio "method ratatui::widgets::Gauge::ratio"). The bar width and height are defined by the [`Rect`](../prelude/struct.Rect.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Rect") it is [rendered](../prelude/trait.Widget.html#tymethod.render "method ratatui::prelude::Widget::render") in.

The associated label is always centered horizontally and vertically. If not set with [`Gauge::label`](struct.Gauge.html#method.label "method ratatui::widgets::Gauge::label"), the label is the percentage of the bar filled.

You might want to have a higher precision bar using [`Gauge::use_unicode`](struct.Gauge.html#method.use_unicode "method ratatui::widgets::Gauge::use_unicode").

This can be useful to indicate the progression of a task, like a download.

## [§](#example)Example

```
use ratatui::style::{Style, Stylize};
use ratatui::widgets::{Block, Gauge};

Gauge::default()
    .block(Block::bordered().title("Progress"))
    .gauge_style(Style::new().white().on_black().italic())
    .percent(20);
```

